State requirements are **capability-aware**. Claim only the states this feature
actually has — inventing an empty state for a screen that cannot be empty
produces a test asserting something impossible, which is worse than no test.

| If the feature has…              | The states to specify                                   |
| -------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------- |
| a data-backed read               | loading, empty, error with retry, success — as applicable |
| a mutation                       | pending, success, business conflict, error — as applicable |
| static or local-only UI          | only the states that genuinely exist                     |

- [ ] AC-0n: data states above are handled for the reads and mutations this
